Well, it's hard experience you gain sitting days in front of the
screen ;-). In short: some corpses are poisonous, some not, some can 
give you 'special effects' (as you notied with floating eyes). 
Poisonous monsters are poisonous always (you may be poison 
resistant - e.g. barbarions are, then you'll not get the poison
effect). Some corpses are acidic - you always loose few HP eating
them but no big harm is done. Corpses that give you extra effects
usually do it only with certain probability. After some time you'll
learn about dungeon cusine enough to know what is safe and what not.
  Aha, remember, that corpses tend to rot - they should be eaten
fresh (zombie corpses are occasionally rotten right away, after you
kill them). This affects almost all the corpses - the symptom is
'you feel deathly sick' message. If not cured quickly (and even 
simple granny's methods can help ;-) the sickness is fatal. 
  And: if you don't like '...tastes terrible' message - polymorph
into a monster. Most corpses will become yummy!

